    "raw_text": "News Releases\nJune 3, 2026\nState Officials and Dairy Leaders Come Together to Celebrate 250 Years of PA Dairy\nHARRISBURG – As the U.S. celebrates its 250th anniversary, Sen. Elder Vogel, Jr. (R-47) and Sen. Judy Schwank (D-11) joined their colleagues and state dairy leaders to honor 250 years of dedication from Pennsylvania’s dairy industry during this year’s National Dairy Month celebration. “With much to be proud of as a commonwealth and as a […]\n[Read More]\nMay 26, 2026\nVogel to Host June 5 Butler County Senior Expo\nSen. Elder Vogel, Jr. (R-47) will host his Butler County Senior Expo on Friday, June 5, from 10 a.m. to 1 p.m. at the Discovery Church, 170 Scharberry Lane in Mars.\n[Read More]\nMay 7, 2026\nVogel, Kinkead Celebrate the 16th Season of the Capitol Hunger Garden\nAs the Penn State Master Gardeners, PA Vegetable Growers Association and volunteers gathered today to begin planting this season’s produce, Sen. Elder Vogel, Jr. (R-47) and Rep. Emily Kinkead (D-20) provided the following statements celebrating the start of the Capitol Hunger Garden’s 16th season.\n[Read More]\nApril 30, 2026\nVogel Announces Environmental Education Funding for Projects in Beaver County\nSen. Elder Vogel, Jr. (R-47) announced today two projects in Beaver County will receive $35,000 in Environmental Education Grants program funding, administered by the state Department of Environmental Protection.\n[Read More]\nApril 15, 2026\nVogel Announces More Than $740,000 in Grants to Help At-Risk Youth\nSen. Elder Vogel, Jr. (R-47) announced today the approval of more than $740,000 in Building Opportunity through Out-of-School Time (BOOST) and Violence Intervention and Prevention (VIP) grants for two projects in the 47th Senatorial District.\n[Read More]\nMarch 6, 2026\nVogel to Host 15th Annual Kids Extravaganza on April 11\nSen. Elder Vogel, Jr. (R-47) will be hosting his 15th Annual Kid’s Extravaganza on Saturday, April 11, from 11 a.m. to 2 p.m., at CCBC – Athletics and Events Center, 1 Campus Drive in Monaca.\n[Read More]\nPosts navigation\nOlder Entries\n2025 News Releases\nVogel Announces State Grants for Municipal Traffic Light Upgrades in Beaver and Butler Counties\nVogel, Matzie: $237,500 in Revitalization Funding Coming to Beaver County\nLocal State Lawmakers Announce $4.6 Million in State Funding for 22 Beaver County Projects\nVogel: Bipartisan Budget Bill Advances Key Investments in Our Schools, Our Workforce and Our Farmers\nContinuing to Help Feed Harrisburg Communities in Need, Capitol Hunger Garden Closes Out Its 15th Season\nVogel, CCBC to Host Veterans Appreciation Breakfast Nov. 6\nVogel Condemns Hateful Political Violence Following Assassination of Charlie Kirk\nVogel, Hunger Caucus Bring Awareness to Hunger in Pennsylvania\nVogel Holding September Food Drive Honoring Hunger Action Month\nVogel Announces $10.3 Million to Expand High-Speed Broadband Access in 47th Senate District\n2024 News Releases\nVogel Announces Funding to Bridge Digital Divide through Device Access in Beaver County\nVogel Announces 11 Projects in Beaver, Butler, and Lawrence Counties will Benefit from Over $9 Million in State Grants\nCapitol Hunger Garden Continues to Provide Fresh Produce for Harrisburg Residents in Need\nVogel Announces More Than $11 Million in State Grants for Beaver, Butler and Lawrence County Projects\nVogel, Kinkead Close Out the Capitol Hunger Garden’s 14th Season\nVogel and Community College of Beaver County to Host Annual Veterans Breakfast\nVogel Announces Investment to Enhance Broadband Access in Beaver County\nVogel to Host Veterans Assistance Specialist in Cranberry Township Office on Oct. 10\nVogel: Food Insecurity Continues to Affect 1.5 Million Pennsylvanians\nVogel, Hunger Caucus to Honor Hunger Action Month on Sept. 17\n2023 News Releases\nVogel to Host Veteran’s Assistance Specialist in Cranberry Township Office on January 5\nVogel Announces Over $10 Million  for Water Infrastructure, Arts and Culture Projects in Beaver, Butler and Lawrence Counties\nVogel Announces Over $1.4 Million in State Funding Awarded for Aliquippa Industrial Park Project\nVogel’s SANE Expansion Legislation Advances to the Governor’s Desk\nVogel’s Dog Law Modernization Bill Signed Into Law\nVogel’s Dog Law Modernization Bill Heads to the Governor’s Desk\nVogel Announces Over $3 Million in Park Project Grants for Beaver, Butler, and Lawrence Counties\nVogel, Kinkead Highlight Positive Impacts of Capitol Hunger Garden as It Closes for the Season\nVogel, Kinkead Highlight Impacts of Capitol Hunger Garden as It Concludes Its 13th Season\nVogel to Host Free Senior Expo Tomorrow, Sept. 29\n2022 News Releases\nKeystone Communities Program Grants Awarded to Beaver, Lawrence Communities\nVogel Announces Beaver County Farm Preserved\nGrants Awarded to Beaver County Law Enforcement Agencies\nBeaver, Butler, Lawrence County Projects Receive Nearly $6.8 Million in RACP Grants\nVogel Named 2022 Rural Health Legislator of the Year\nBeaver, Butler County Projects Receive a Combined Total in Excess of $7.2 Million\nBrooks, Vogel Announce $3.5 Million Grant to Create Local Jobs at Steelite\nEllwood City Receives Nearly $6 Million in PENNVEST Funding\n**MEDIA ADVISORY**  Tuesday Event to Highlight Hunger Garden 12th Season, Hunger Action Month Food Drive Results\nMore than $318,000 in Grant Funding Distributed to Area Outdoor Recreation Projects",
