    "raw_text": "Be Aware of Dirty Dirt\nPublic Hearing on future of the Over Order Premium on Class I Milk\nAgriculture & Rural Affairs Committee, Chair\nDairy Across the Commonwealth\nRecent News\nE-news Updates – June 28, 2026\nE-news Updates – June 14, 2026\nState Officials and Dairy Leaders Come Together to Celebrate 250 Years of PA Dairy\nmedia_file= 1198090138\nCelebrating Dairy Month in PA\nmedia_file= 1197799478\nMeeting to consider SB 866\nE-news Updates – May 31, 2026\nSee More\nseneldervogel\n1,305\nIt was great to join so many friends and neighbors at this year`s Beaver County BOOM 250 celebration!\nThank you to everyone who helped make this event such a success. The evening was capped off with an incredible fireworks display by Zambelli Fireworks—a spectacular way to celebrate America`s 250th anniversary and the pride we share in our community.\n3\n0\nOpen post by seneldervogel with ID 17896061688512738\nIt was great to join so many friends and neighbors at this year`s Beaver County BOOM 250 celebration!\nThank you to everyone who helped make this event such a success. The evening was capped off with an incredible fireworks display by Zambelli Fireworks—a spectacular way to celebrate America`s 250th anniversary and the pride we share in our community.\n...\n3\n0\nThe PA State Police Cadet selection cycle is open through July 31 for men and women considering a career in law enforcement. Find out how to take the first step here: https://bit.ly/4oAwKzC\n0\n0\nOpen post by seneldervogel with ID 17944737789219044\nThe PA State Police Cadet selection cycle is open through July 31 for men and women considering a career in law enforcement. Find out how to take the first step here: https://bit.ly/4oAwKzC\n...\n0\n0\nLast weekend, I was honored to attend the Baden Past, Present & Future America 250 Years celebration. It was a great opportunity to reflect on the values that have shaped our nation over the last 250 years and continue to strengthen our communities today.\n3\n0\nOpen post by seneldervogel with ID 18006345413747556\nLast weekend, I was honored to attend the Baden Past, Present & Future America 250 Years celebration. It was a great opportunity to reflect on the values that have shaped our nation over the last 250 years and continue to strengthen our communities today.\n...\n3\n0\nThe 2027 Statewide Transportation Improvement Program, a list of PA projects identified for funding, is available for public review until June 30. You can review the plan and submit your comments to Pennsylvania Department of Transportation (PennDOT) here: https://bit.ly/4uO5Tlj\n0\n1\nOpen post by seneldervogel with ID 18136019611566499\nThe 2027 Statewide Transportation Improvement Program, a list of PA projects identified for funding, is available for public review until June 30. You can review the plan and submit your comments to Pennsylvania Department of Transportation (PennDOT) here: https://bit.ly/4uO5Tlj\n...\n0\n1\nYou can show off your photography skills and celebrate PA agriculture by entering the Pennsylvania Department of Agriculture  Photo Contest by June 30. Submit up to four original photos highlighting the people, places, traditions and beauty of PA farming. Find details here: https://bit.ly/4erahR4\n2\n0\nOpen post by seneldervogel with ID 17930049528341733\nYou can show off your photography skills and celebrate PA agriculture by entering the Pennsylvania Department of Agriculture  Photo Contest by June 30. Submit up to four original photos highlighting the people, places, traditions and beauty of PA farming. Find details here: https://bit.ly/4erahR4\n...\n2\n0\nThis past weekend, I was honored to attend the Opening Ceremony of the Harmony Township America 250 Celebration, \"Diplomacy to Defense.\"\nAs we begin commemorating our nation`s 250th anniversary, we took time to remember and honor the 17 Revolutionary War soldiers laid to rest at this historic site. Their service and sacrifice helped secure the freedoms we enjoy today.\nIt was a meaningful opportunity to reflect on our nation`s founding and recognize the important role Harmony Township played in our early American history. Thank you to everyone who helped organize this special event and preserve the stories that continue to shape our community and country.\n0\n0\nOpen post by seneldervogel with ID 18084834035552997\nThis past weekend, I was honored to attend the Opening Ceremony of the Harmony Township America 250 Celebration, \"Diplomacy to Defense.\"\nAs we begin commemorating our nation`s 250th anniversary, we took time to remember and honor the 17 Revolutionary War soldiers laid to rest at this historic site. Their service and sacrifice helped secure the freedoms we enjoy today.\nIt was a meaningful opportunity to reflect on our nation`s founding and recognize the important role Harmony Township played in our early American history. Thank you to everyone who helped organize this special event and preserve the stories that continue to shape our community and country.\n...\n0\n0\nThe Center for Dairy Excellence serves as a one-stop-shop for strengthening our state`s dairy industry! They provide essential resources and beneficial programs as well as positive outreach opportunities to best assist farmers and inform the public! Learn more: www.centerfordairyexcellence.org\n0\n0\nOpen post by seneldervogel with ID 17879387838608655\nThe Center for Dairy Excellence serves as a one-stop-shop for strengthening our state`s dairy industry! They provide essential resources and beneficial programs as well as positive outreach opportunities to best assist farmers and inform the public! Learn more: www.centerfordairyexcellence.org\n...\n0\n0\nHappy Father’s Day to all the dads, grandfathers, stepfathers, and father figures across our communities.\nToday, we celebrate the men who lead by example, provide guidance, offer support, and make countless sacrifices for their families. Thank you for the love, dedication, and values you pass on to the next generation.\nWishing everyone a happy and blessed Father’s Day spent with family and loved ones.\n0\n0\nOpen post by seneldervogel with ID 18100546739518979\nHappy Father’s Day to all the dads, grandfathers, stepfathers, and father figures across our communities.\nToday, we celebrate the men who lead by example, provide guidance, offer support, and make countless sacrifices for their families. Thank you for the love, dedication, and values you pass on to the next generation.\nWishing everyone a happy and blessed Father’s Day spent with family and loved ones.\n...\n0\n0\nLoad More\nFollow on Instagram\nConnect With Us\nHarrisburg\nSenate Box 203047\n286 Main Capitol Building\nHarrisburg, PA 17120-3047\nPhone:\n(717) 787-3076\nFAX: (717) 772-2756\nTTY – Use 711 (\nexplained here\n)\nRochester\n488 Adams St.\nRochester, PA 15074-1940\nPhone:\n(724) 774-0444\nFAX: (724) 773-7384\nCranberry Township\n8001 Rowan Road, Suite 205\nCranberry Township, PA 16066\nPhone:\n(878) 978-2575\nFAX: (878) 978-2464\nMore Information\nFacebook Feed\nElder Vogel Jr.\nMeet Elder Vogel, Jr.\nFrom being a lifelong farmer and a local township supervisor to being elected to serve the 47th Senatorial District, Sen. Elder Vogel, Jr. continues to advocate for the interests important to his fellow residents. He serves as a fierce agricultural leader within the Senate and champions vital measures like access expansion for telemedicine and sexual assault nurse practitioners in Pennsylvania. When he’s not in Harrisburg, you’ll find him visiting community events or working on his family farm (est. in 1873).\nLearn More",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Senator Elder Vogel Jr. attended several local community events in his district, including America 250th anniversary celebrations in Beaver County, Baden, and Harmony Township. He also shared informational posts about the PA State Police cadet application cycle, a PennDOT transportation funding plan open for public comment, and a Pennsylvania Department of Agriculture photo contest. No new legislation or formal government actions are described in this release.",
