  {
    "title": "VISIT THE CAPITOL",
    "url": "https://www.pacapitol.com/plan-a-visit/",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Plan a Visit - PA Capitol\nThe Pennsylvania Capitol\nA National Historic Landmark\nPlan a Visit\nVideo Tours\nEvents\n- opens in a new tab\nEducation\nThe General Assembly\n- opens in a new tab\nBOOK A TOUR\nVisit The Capitol\nEverything you need to know about visiting the Capitol.\nVisitor Services\nJust have a question? Look no further. We're here to help.\nHome\nPlan a Visit\nCapitol Tours\n*All tours on October 17, 2026 have been cancelled. We sincerely apologize for any inconvenience and appreciate your understanding.\nYour safety is important to us. We ask that you comply with the following guidelines.\nTours fill quickly. We recommend scheduling in advance.\nWalk-ins are welcome according to availability.\nArrive 15 minutes prior to your tour time and check in with the guide at the information desk.\nTours take approximately 30-45 minutes.\nOur tours are limited to 40 guests total per tour. Book your tour online at\nwww.pacapitol.com.\nAs a reminder self- guided tours are\nnot\npermitted weekends and holidays.\nHave a great day!\n-From all of the Capitol Tour Guides!\nPlan a Visit\nThe Pennsylvania State Capitol building is a functional seat of government, where laws are passed and\r\n    the public policy is set for over 13 million residents of Pennsylvania. Visitors are welcome to explore\r\n    the Capitol Building at their leisure, on regular weekdays. Leave plenty of time to visit\r\n    our\nInteractive Welcome Center\nand\nCapitol Gift Shop\n.\nTours are limited to 40 people total per tour. Groups with more than 40 people\r\n        will require multiple tour times. Please schedule accordingly\nVisitors must use the public entrances - East Wing Entrance at the Fountain on Commonwealth Avenue (also the ADA compliant entrance),\r\n    and the Main Rotunda Entrance at Third and State Streets (\nview map\n).\r\n    For more on security at the Capitol, please\nclick here\nfor more information on security at the Capitol\n.\nPlanning a visit on a weekend or holiday?\nClick here for important information\non visiting on a holiday or weekend\n.\nParking/Directions\nLocated in center-city Harrisburg, there are many ways to get to the Capitol and several parking opportunities.\nInteractive Welcome Center\nWe invite you to explore all things Pennsylvania by visiting the Interactive Welcome center, located in the East Wing, at the Capitol. Open regular weekdays 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\nSenate Library Exhibits\nJourney from the Senate of the past to the Senate of today through these exhibits.\n- opens in a new tab\nCapitol Events\nFind out the latest on what's going on at the Capitol.\n- opens in a new tab\nThe Capitol Complex\nThe Pennsylvania State Capitol Complex is comprised of the buildings owned by the Commonwealth and are centered around the Capitol in Harrisburg.\nCapitol Shop\nWhen visiting Pennsylvania's Capitol, be sure to stop by The Pennsylvania Capitol Shop, located off the East Wing Rotunda. The Capitol Gift Shop is open 9:30 a.m. - 3:30 p.m. (regular Weekdays)\nCapitol Guided Tours\nTake a free tour guided by one of our Capitol History specialists.\nWatching Session\nInformation for watching House or Senate session.\nCapitol Tour Etiquette\nThings to keep in mind while touring the Capitol.\nAccessibility Services\nInformation on wheelchair and ADA compliant parking availability.\nArea Attractions\nAs you plan your visit to the Pennsylvania State Capitol, be sure to consider other local attractions.\nWhere to Eat\nThe Capitol Restaurant is a cafeteria style eatery located on the concourse level of the East Wing.\nTouring Tips\nSome tips and hints to get the most of your Capitol touring experience.\nKeystone Classroom\nInformation and printable publications that you may find helpful, whether you're planning to visit the Capitol or teaching Pennsylvania history.\nMaps\nMaps of the Capitol Building and Capitol Complex\nFrequently Asked Questions\nSome answers to the most commonly asked questions.\nWhat our visitors are saying?\nOur tour guide was absolutely lovely! Not only did she share the history of the building, but she also had a deep knowledge of the art, architecture, and symbolism that the building was filled with. We also loved hearing about her personal stories and her clear love for her job. Overall, just fantastic!\n1 year ago \r\n                                    (via The PA Capitol Tour Survey)\nI enjoyed getting to learn all about our Capitol building and getting to see how beautiful the architecture is! Our tour guide was WONDERFUL, so knowledgeable and gave a wonderful tour.\n1 year ago \r\n                                    (via The PA Capitol Tour Survey)\nSo informative above and beyond the politics that go on inside the Capitol Building\n1 year ago \r\n                                    (via The PA Capitol Tour Survey)\nExtremely knowledgeable, friendly and professional tour guide.\n1 year ago \r\n                                    (via The PA Capitol Tour Survey)\nTour Guide is so friendly and gives facts about the capitol to accommodate the ages of the students.\n1 year ago \r\n  ",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "This is not a legislator press release. It is an informational webpage from the Pennsylvania Capitol visitor services office describing how the public can tour the State Capitol building in Harrisburg. It provides practical details such as tour hours, capacity limits, entrance locations, parking, and accessibility information.",
      "action_type": "other",
      "topics": [
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
